    },
    {
      "block_id": 8,
      "type": 0,
      "text": "TELLING THE SYSTEM HOW TO FETCH AND DISPLAY DATA\n",
      "bbox": [
        85.51300048828125,
        295.26385498046875,
        410.7714538574219,
        305.76385498046875
      ],
      "bbox_norm": [
        0.14232478081316344,
        0.3825255909113697,
        0.6836733221935516,
        0.39612874157413897
      ]
    },
    {
      "block_id": 9,
      "type": 0,
      "text": "After defining the size and position of the display window, you need to give the system the on­\nscreen location for data fetched from memory. To do this, you describe the horizontal positions \nwhere each line starts and stops and write these positions to the data-fetch registers. The data- \nfetch registers have a four-pixel resolution (unlike the display window registers, which have a \none-pixel resolution). Each position specified is four pixels from the last one. Pixel 0 is position \n0; pixel 4 is position 1, and so on.\n",
      "bbox": [
        85.26300048828125,
        328.51385498046875,
        518.51220703125,
        403.2078552246094
      ],
      "bbox_norm": [
        0.14190868975098433,
        0.42560223467680575,
        0.8629931799058492,
        0.5223711621935649
      ]
    },
    {
      "block_id": 10,
      "type": 0,
      "text": "The data-fetch start and display window starting positions interact with each other. It is recom­\nmended that data-fetch start values be restricted to a programming resolution of 16 pixels (8 \nclocks in low-resolution mode, 4 clocks in high-resolution mode). The hardware requires some \ntime after the first data fetch before it can actually display the data. As a result, there is a \ndifference between the value of window start and data-fetch start of 4.5 color clocks.\n",
      "bbox": [
        85.06300354003906,
        418.3568420410156,
        518.4719848632812,
        480.6408996582031
      ],
      "bbox_norm": [
        0.14157582198047766,
        0.5419972526746965,
        0.8629262355674762,
        0.6226886259751921
      ]
    },
    {
      "block_id": 11,
      "type": 0,
      "text": "The normal low-resolution DDFSTRT is ($0038).\nThe normal high-resolution DDFSTRT is (S003C).\n",
      "bbox": [
        120.56100463867188,
        495.6408996582031,
        344.90411376953125,
        518.9909057617188
      ],
      "bbox_norm": [
        0.20065742590993763,
        0.6421216983505769,
        0.5740460761932219,
        0.6723725222555964
      ]
    },
    {
      "block_id": 12,
      "type": 0,
      "text": "Recall that the hardware resolution of display window start and stop is twice the hardware resolu­\ntion of data fetch:\n",
      "bbox": [
